From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:00:10 -0500
Subject: feat: bring Arc's pinned folders in pinned

A top-level folder can join a Space's pinned run (folders F38), and a sidebar
file Stedding wrote already brought one back there. Arc's own lists did not
follow: a list of Arc's pinned section came in under the Clear line with plain
tabs, so a pin after it was drawn before it.

A list of the pinned section is now a folder of the run, as a file's is. Every
tab under it, its nested lists' included, is a Space pin with its home, Arc's
nested lists stay folders inside it, and the folder keeps Arc's order among the
pins. The Space need not be the one on screen. A tab Arc adds to such a list
later joins it as a pin, as before. A folder an earlier import left under the
line keeps its place: an import does not move what is already here.

Why: today's Arc data has this shape, and people leaving Arc meet the import
first (BACKLOG S-107, import I3).

Removable when: Arc's files are gone from people's computers.
